# Review routing per governance/decision-rights.md.
#
# As shipped, every privileged path routes to @swampratnz, the sole
# maintainer of this source repo. That is one person holding every
# governance role, which is ZERO separation of duties. It is correct only
# for a single-maintainer repo. Before you rely on this in an org, split
# these across at least three distinct humans: the security/identity owner
# (/registry/), the shared services maintainer (/schemas/, /scripts/,
# /workflows/, /specs/TEMPLATE.md), and the governance/leadership approver
# (/governance/, /docs/plan.md). CODEOWNERS enforcement (a branch-protection
# setting, see docs/platform-hardening.md) is what turns this file from
# advice into a required-review gate.

# Security/identity owner: agent registry, credential lifecycle, frozen instruments
/registry/            @swampratnz

# Shared services maintainer: platform defaults, templates, validator, shared workflows
/schemas/             @swampratnz
/scripts/             @swampratnz
/workflows/           @swampratnz
/specs/TEMPLATE.md    @swampratnz

# Governance changes are chairman/leadership-level review
/governance/          @swampratnz
/docs/plan.md         @swampratnz

# Individual specs are owned by their frontmatter `owner`; CODEOWNERS can't
# express per-file YAML, so add per-team lines here as teams onboard, e.g.:
# /specs/example-team/  @alice
